-- title:
--   Both crossing generic points lie over the smooth locus
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero natural number $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, together with a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ such that every unit $u \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ whose image under the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial already lies in $H$ (with $M/p$ nonzero). Assume the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ`, namely $q^{-1}$ times the integral power series $j$-numerator over $\mathbb{Q}$, lies in the intermediate field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` generated by the integral form ratios for $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for the two-chart integral model $X$ of level $\Gamma_M(M,H)$ over $R_p$ (a bundle recording properness, flatness, integrality and local finite presentation of the structure map `toBase`, normality on affine opens, properness and relative-dimension-one smoothness at level $\Gamma_N$, a geometric curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ identified with the base change together with its Galois and $q$-expansion compatibilities, and smoothness and geometric integrality of the generic fibre). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho \colon R_p \to A$ be a ring homomorphism whose composite with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map of $R_p$. Let $O$ be a commutative ring with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O \colon R_p \to O$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa \colon O \to \kappa_A$ to the residue field of $A$ with $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O$ equal to the composite of $\rho$ with the residue map. Then both points $\mathfrak{X}.\xi_\infty$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\xi_0$ attached to this data in the fibre product of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` with $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho_O)$ lie in the preimage, under the first projection of that fibre product, of the open subset $\mathfrak{X}$.`smoothLocus` of $X$.
--
--   This is the statement that the two generic points of the geometric special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$, viewed in the base change along $\rho_O$, avoid the crossings and hence map into the smooth locus; crossings are closed points and there are only finitely many of them, while each component carries infinitely many closed points. It is used in the computation identifying the sum of the branch ideals at $\xi_\infty$ and $\xi_0$ with the maximal ideal.
